                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>- The Y-axis shows the number of incidents (Count) within each loss range.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>- Each segment of a bar, represented by a different color, corresponds to a different attack type (such as DDoS, Malware, Phishing, Ransomware, SQL Injection, etc.).</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>This chart displays the distribution of various cyberattack incidents across different financial loss ranges from 2015 to 2024. Although it is commonly believed that high-loss ranges are primarily caused by DDoS and malware attacks, the data in this chart indicate that the distribution of all attack types in high-loss ranges is quite balanced. Therefore, whether it is DDoS, malware, phishing, or SQL injection, each carries the potential risk of incurring significant financial losses. This serves as a reminder that while large-scale attack events, though less frequent, can have a substantial financial impact, the cumulative effect of numerous small- and medium-scale incidents should not be overlooked.</run>
                  </formatted-text>
